WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.380
- I always like to finish up

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.420
with something that could
put a smile on your face.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.530
This is What I'm Liking.
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.810
A Pacific Northwest artist
is spreading the message

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.660
that disabilities don't have
to hold you back from anything.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.620
Even though he's blind,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.830
he does incredible woodwork
just by sound and feel.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.180
It's incredible!

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.520
And he's turned it into a full-time job.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.940
He details it all in his TikTok
channel, The Blind Woodsman,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.490
and people are fascinated,
as they should be.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.680
He's got nearly 2 million followers.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.030
We have him on the line right now,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.710
watching on Fox 12, Oregon.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.510
Everybody say hi to John!

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.571
- [All] What's up, John!
(audience cheering)

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:38.037
- [Kelly] Oh my!
(John laughs)

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.440
- I'm having a good day
up here in Washington.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.273
How are you?

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:43.320
- Oh my God, I love Washington!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.110
So wait, you've been a
woodworker for 15 years, right?

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.160
- That's right.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.310
I was kind of having a
hard time finding my place

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.080
in the world and what I was gonna do

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.550
and I started attending a
woodshop at a Center for the Blind

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.320
in Salt Lake City, Utah,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.100
and I found immediately that
I really had a knack for it.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.200
I really understood it well,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.350
and so, for the next couple of years,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.210
I had actually become close friends

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.710
with the woodshop teacher,

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.450
and so I just kind of spent
the next few years honing

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.300
my woodworking skills
and that kind of a thing,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.750
and now I am a professional artist

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.520
and I make functional art,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.030
like bowls, cups, plates,
canisters, those kind of things.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.658
- I mean,
(audience applauds)

00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:30.453
your work is incredible, man!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.740
I mean, congratulations on like, you know,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.170
starting this and just killing it.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.880
Like, it's incredible, your work.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.670
So, tell us about your TikTok videos.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:46.290
- Okay, so we like to make
videos about educating people

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.253
about blindness and disabilities
and things like that.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.670
We wanna show 'em that
we're just regular people,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.630
like anybody else.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.870
We can do things if we put our mind to it.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:01.080
And I also like to show my process,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.330
like my adaptive measuring tool

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.140
and how I use that and
the way I use the tools.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.640
I also have to say that I
definitely do not do this alone.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.590
My wife, Anni, who is also
a very talented artist,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.270
she does all the technical stuff.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.158
I just make stuff and
look pretty. (laughs)

00:02:22.158 --> 00:02:22.991
(audience laughs)

00:02:22.991 --> 00:02:24.150
And we truly believe

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.783
that when you dispel ignorance,
fear and hatred go away.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.150
- Oh, absolutely.
(audience cheering)

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.340
Well, you sent me one
of your latest projects.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.420
I cannot wait.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.150
This is so beautiful!

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:40.353
And the detail y'all.
(audience cheering)

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:42.660
I am so impressed by you.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.460
Like, this is so incredible.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.610
It must feel so good to be able
to make something like this.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.800
Thank you so much for this

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.020
and John, you're just incredible.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.610
You're such an inspiration.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.110
We love you joining the show today.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.591
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:56.591 --> 00:02:58.350
(heart dings)
(audience clapping)

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.800
- [John] Thank you very much!

00:03:02.372 --> 00:03:03.205
Thank you for the opportunity.

00:03:03.205 --> 00:03:04.038
- Oh, absolutely.

00:03:04.038 --> 00:03:04.871
Well, hey, that's not all.

00:03:04.871 --> 00:03:06.390
Our season long partner,
Pilot, pen makers of FriXion,

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.760
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.740
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.080
and spreading positivity
just like you, my man.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.000
So, they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.045
How's that sound?

00:03:16.045 --> 00:03:17.317
(audience cheering)

00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:18.210
- Oh wow!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.053
Thank you!

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.093
That's amazing!

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.603
I'll definitely be going
down to the wood store.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.060
- Thank you so much, John

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.804
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:29.804 --> 00:03:31.394
Awkwafina, Charles Esten, Cindy, and Amy.

00:03:31.394 --> 00:03:32.754
Y'all have a great day, and if it's not,

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:33.806
try and change it.

